'''Pets''' are companions that can be summoned, giving bonus [[Stats]] and one or more different perks. They can be accessed and managed in the Pets Menu, which can be accessed through the [[SkyBlock Menu]].

__TOC__

The stats and perks that a Pet gives are dependent on its '''level''' and '''rarity'''. Most pets have a specific [[Skills|Skill]] attributed to them. Pets can level up by gaining Skill XP, and they gain the most Skill XP when the player gains XP for its attributed Skill (i.e. a {{Item|Zombie Pet}} would gain the most XP from {{Skill|Combat}}, a {{Item|Rabbit Pet}} would gain the most XP from {{Skill|Farming}}, etc.). Most pets belong to one of {{Green|9}} skills: {{Skl|Combat}}, {{Skl|Mining}}, {{Skl|Fishing}}, {{Skl|Foraging}}, {{Skl|Farming}}, {{Skl|Enchanting}}, {{Skl|Alchemy}}, {{Skl|Taming}}, and {{Skl|Hunting}}. The {{Item|Bingo Pet}} and {{Item|Precursor Drone Pet}} are <u>All Skills</u> pets. The [[File:Droplet Wisp Pet.png|21px|link=Wisp Pet]] [[Wisp Pet]] is a <u>Gabagool</u> pet, and the {{Item|Montezuma Pet}} is a <u>Fractured Soul</u> pet. Gabagool Pets are leveled up by being fed [[Gabagool (disambiguation)|Gabagool]].

Pets can be obtained in multiple ways:
* Crafting, through the use of an {{Item|Egg}}, {{Item|Enchanted Egg}}, {{Item|Super Enchanted Egg}}, or {{Item|Omega Enchanted Egg}};
* Mob drops, from mobs like {{MobSprite|Ender Dragon}}s, {{MobSprite|Scatha}}s, {{MobSprite|Yeti}}s, or {{MobSprite|Loch Emperor}}s, which are affected by {{Stat|mf}} and {{Stat|pl}};
* Purchasing, from places like the [[Dark Auction]] or specific merchants;
* Forging, through [[The Forge]];
* Milestone rewards, such as {{Skill|Mining}}, {{Skill|Fishing}}, and the [[Kuudra]] boss collection.

Most pets that are crafted start at {{Common}}, and must be upgraded through {{NPCSprite|Kat}}; however, some pets only start at certain rarities, like {{Rare}} or {{Epic}}. Some pets can be upgraded to {{Mythic}} at {{NPCSprite|Kat}}, and will need a special item to upgrade.

== Pets Menu ==
The '''Pets Menu''' can be opened by using the [[Command]]s {{Code|/viewpetsmenu}}, {{Code|/petsmenu}}, {{Code|/petmenu}}, {{Code|/pets}} (empty by default), or by accessing it from the [[SkyBlock Menu]]. Here, players can view and manage their pets, view their Pet Score and Autopet rules, and manage more options.

'''Pets Menu''' can hold a maximum of {{Green|112}} pets by default. It can be upgraded with {{Bits|5,000}} to unlock {{Green|28}} more slots. This upgrade can be bought twice.

{{/UI}}

